From: cubie-a5e-openwrt <noreply@github.com>
Subject: arm64: dts: allwinner: a527-cubie-a5e: Wi-Fi power sequence

ImmortalWrt's 131-01 adds the mmc1 node and the PL7 3.3 V switch for the
AIC8800D80 module. Two more bits come from the Radxa BSP device tree
(radxa/allwinner-device, configs/cubie_a5e/linux-5.15/board.dts):

 - WL_REG_ON is PM1 ("wlan_regon = <&r_pio PM 1 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>"):
   drive it with mmc-pwrseq-simple instead of relying on its state after
   U-Boot. Armbian (patch 22-Enable-wifi-on-Radxa-Cubie-A5E) does the same.
 - the module's I/O runs from BLDO1 (1.8 V, "vcc-pg-iowifi"; the BSP uses
   it as vqmmc of sdc1): name it as vqmmc so it is never switched off
   while mmc1 is in use.

Not yet verified on hardware.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-a527-cubie-a5e.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-a527-cubie-a5e.dts
index ee7b254..8245bf2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-a527-cubie-a5e.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-a527-cubie-a5e.dts
@@ -61,6 +61,16 @@
 		enable-active-high;
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * WL_REG_ON of the AIC8800D80 module is PM1 (wlan_regon in the
+	 * Radxa BSP device tree); toggled once on power-up.
+	 */
+	wifi_pwrseq: wifi-pwrseq {
+		compatible = "mmc-pwrseq-simple";
+		reset-gpios = <&r_pio 1 1 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>; /* PM1 */
+		post-power-on-delay-ms = <200>;
+	};
+
 	reg_vcc5v: vcc5v {
 		/* board wide 5V supply from the USB-C connector */
 		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
@@ -224,6 +234,8 @@
 
 &mmc1 {
 	vmmc-supply = <&reg_3v3_wifi>;
+	vqmmc-supply = <&reg_bldo1>;
+	mmc-pwrseq = <&wifi_pwrseq>;
 	bus-width = <4>;
 	non-removable;
 	// todo: investigate why clock above 40MHz makes data errors
